**Issue**: #276
**Date**: 2026-08-26
**Status**: Approved
**Author**: NMG

@issue-276 @bug @write-spec
Feature: Resolve write-spec templates from their packaged workflow bundle
  Installed write-spec sessions must load every specification template from
  the owning workflow directory instead of a nonexistent package-root folder.

  Scenario: Installed workflow names every bundled template explicitly
    Given nmg-sdlc is installed under an OMP plugin root
    When the write-spec workflow reaches template loading
    Then it reads "workflows/write-spec/templates/requirements.md"
    And it reads "workflows/write-spec/templates/design.md"
    And it reads "workflows/write-spec/templates/tasks.md"
    And it reads "workflows/write-spec/templates/feature.gherkin"
    And it does not read a package-root "templates/" directory

  Scenario: Prompt contract rejects the ambiguous template lookup
    Given the write-spec interactive-plan contract test
    When the workflow source is evaluated
    Then all four explicit packaged template paths are required
    And the obsolete "Use templates from templates/" instruction is absent

  Scenario: Corrected workflow passes repository verification
    Given the write-spec workflow bundle and issue 276 spec
    When focused and applicable repository gates run
    Then the workflow contract passes
    And bundle validation passes
    And the user-visible correction is recorded in the release changelog
